task: growing
agent: opus5-intent
started: 2026-09-07
branch: feature/growing
worktree: ../okay-wt-grow

why: the operator's decision (2026-09-07), after I measured the design
  and reverted it: keep what was built and improve it from there. My
  objection was that it is dominated at every producer count and a
  knob that is never best misleads; the operator has decided, so the
  objection goes where it belongs — into the doc beside the knob, as
  the measured table, so the choice is made with the numbers rather
  than instead of them.

what: restore `Growing` at its last state (sampled producer identity
  as the trigger, refusal handled on the channel's own
  `pushDecidingAt`), its four laws, the `Queues.strong[A].growing`
  builder, the `AdaptiveFifo(first, firstOwner)` adoption it needs,
  and the `growing_chunk` lane. Document what it costs and what it
  buys at one, four and sixteen producers, and say plainly that today
  it is a starting point rather than the best choice at any count.

predict: the numbers are the ones already measured (158 / 477 / 446
  against the ring's 123 / 715 / 3 066), because this is the same code
  — this lane adds no optimisation, only the honest surface. The next
  lane is `queue-swap`'s remaining six steps, which is where the two
  layers become one.
